  Two things to be aware of:

  - [1mSQLite version.[0m You didn't specify a target, so I used the plain [38;5;153mDROP COLUMN[39m form, which needs SQLite 3.35.0+
    (released March 2021). My local sqlite3 is 3.51.0. If production runs anything older, this migration fails on apply
    and needs the table-rebuild approach instead — worth a quick check against whatever the deploy job runs.
  - [1mThe write path.[0m You said you think the app no longer writes to [38;5;153mnotes[39m. I only looked at this repo, which is
    schema-only — no application code here — so I couldn't confirm that. If any code still references the column, it
    breaks the moment this migration lands. Worth a grep across the app repo before the deploy job picks this up.

